A Pilot reviews the flight plan and requests clarification from operations before departure.
A Pilot reports an in-flight technical irregularity to maintenance after landing.
A Pilot submits feedback on route conditions to the scheduling team for future adjustments.

A Flight Attendant prepares the cabin and checks safety equipment before boarding starts.
A Flight Attendant files a passenger incident report to the cabin services supervisor after arrival.
A Flight Attendant confirms special-assistance passengers with the ground crew before boarding.

An Operations Coordinator assigns aircraft to scheduled flights based on availability and maintenance status.
An Operations Coordinator manages a last-minute gate change and informs all relevant teams.
An Operations Coordinator issues a disruption notice to customer service when delays exceed a threshold.

A Maintenance Engineer performs a routine inspection and updates the aircraft’s maintenance record.
A Maintenance Engineer addresses a reported technical issue and releases the aircraft back into service.
A Maintenance Engineer flags an aircraft for extended maintenance and notifies operations to reassign flights.

A Customer Service Agent assists passengers with rebooking options after a disruption notice.
A Customer Service Agent verifies travel documents at the check-in counter and reports inconsistencies to security.
A Customer Service Agent coordinates with baggage services to locate and forward missing luggage.